    "done_when": "Per the plan's section 4 and decision cryostat-in-both-phases. (1) imas_ambix/data/selene_deck.py: EQSLE.DATA's NV=120 passive block is written as two named pf_passive loops, VV (the first resistivity group, deck lines 293-355, 63 filaments at 7.76e-7 ohm m) and CRYOSTAT (the second group, lines 356-412, 57 slabs at 7.20e-7 ohm m), with filaments named VV_1 onward and CRYOSTAT_1 onward. The converter refuses to label a group CRYOSTAT unless every one of its filaments lies outside the vessel group's R and Z envelope. OP2 carries its own vessel from coil_vv_OP2.dat as loop VV (98) plus the same CRYOSTAT loop read from EQSLE.DATA, so the two phases' CRYOSTAT loops are identical. (2) The OP1 wall: the deck's segment list is split by its labels, so the first-wall segments form the single limiter unit (wall/description_2d/limiter/unit/outline), and the VV inner and outer skins become one vessel unit's annular outline_inner and outline_outer (wall/description_2d/vessel/unit/annular). OP2's limiter keeps its single outline from coil_vv_OP2.dat, and OP2 gets a vessel unit only if its source carries skins. Tests in tests/data/test_selene_deck.py assert the loop names and counts, the envelope refusal, a limiter that is one closed contour, and the vessel unit's two outlines. (3) Re-convert OP1 and OP2 from the sha256-verified copies in /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/ (refuse on any sha256 that differs from /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/source/provenance.json). Record every existing file's sha256 first, and write each new file under a temporary name in the same directory, then rename it into place, because a peer session's figures read this store. Read every file back through imas.DBEntry at DD 4.1.1. (4) imas_ambix/data/machine_maps/jt-60sa.json declares the pf_passive families as VV and CRYOSTAT in both maps, and binds the wall limiter and vessel units as the store now carries them, edited line by line rather than re-serialised whole. tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py asserts OP1 VV 63, OP2 VV 98 and CRYOSTAT 57 in both. Its boundary test asserts that pf_passive VV and the wall differ across 101173/101174, while the CRYOSTAT loop, pf_active and magnetics are byte-equal. This session runs inside the fleet SLURM allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID is set), so the gate runs in place: TMPDIR=/tmp UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider -n 8 tests/data/test_selene_deck.py tests/data/test_jt60sa_machine_map.py tests/data/test_description_reader.py tests/data/test_description_identity.py tests/data/test_transform_engine.py > <your log> 2>&1; echo EXIT=$?, exiting 0, with the gate log's first line naming the revision, the tree and the command. UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/imas-ambix/.venv PYTHONPATH=$PWD command uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. The evidence fragment docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-passive-cryostat-and-wall.html records the replaced and new sha256 per phase and file, the loop names and counts, and the limiter point count per phase. Nothing outside /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP1 and /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description/OP2 is written under /work/projects/imas_gpu/jt60sa/machine_description, and the JT-60SA server is never contacted (no ssh jt-60sa, no EDDB call).",
